WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
SAST in CI/CD should provide timely feedback while preserving accountability and judgment.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.700
Branch and pull request scanning can focus on new or changed code.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.640
Incremental scans can shorten feedback loops.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.140
Full scans can run on a schedule or before major releases.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:25.000
Quality gates and severity thresholds can prevent high-risk issues from moving forward, but they should be designed with enough context to avoid unnecessary blockage.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.300
Baseline scans are useful when adopting SAST on an existing codebase.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.920
They establish known findings so the team can distinguish new issues from inherited debt.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.100
A baseline does not make old risk disappear.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:45.240
It creates a manageable path: prevent new high-risk issues, plan remediation for existing issues, and measure whether the backlog is improving.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.940
Without this strategy, teams may respond by ignoring the tool entirely.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.240
Exception workflows need ownership.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:59.900
Sometimes a finding cannot be fixed immediately, is not reachable, is mitigated by another control, or requires a larger design change.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.240
Exceptions should be justified, documented, reviewed, assigned, and revisited.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:11.940
Suppression without process can hide real risk; exception management with evidence can support informed release decisions.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.400
Automation should not hide responsibility.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:22.220
Developer notifications, tracking unresolved findings, release risk review, and audit trails help teams understand what happened and why.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.960
Break-the-build decisions should be predictable enough that developers trust them.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.820
The purpose of pipeline integration is not punishment.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:35.120
It is consistent, early, actionable feedback that helps teams release software with fewer avoidable risks.
